PASS  /db answers 200
PASS  /db carries Server, Date and application/json
PASS  /db is one {id, randomNumber} object
PASS  /db's number is the row's
PASS  /queries?queries=20 answers 20 rows, each the row's
PASS  a query with no count answers 1 row
PASS  an empty count answers 1 row
PASS  a count of 0 answers 1 row
PASS  a negative count answers 1 row
PASS  a count that is not a number answers 1 row
PASS  a count of 500 answers 500 rows
PASS  a count of 501 answers 500 rows
PASS  a count past i32 answers 500 rows
PASS  five clients' 20 rows each are answered
PASS  their 100 keys ride fewer executions than five
PASS  one execution carries keys of more than one request
PASS  /cached-queries?count=10 answers 10 rows, each the row's
PASS  a cached query with no count answers 1 row
PASS  a cached count of 0 answers 1 row
PASS  a cached count that is not a number answers 1 row
PASS  a cached count of 501 answers 500 rows
PASS  a cached query reads no row from the database
PASS  /updates?queries=20 answers 20 rows, each the row as written
PASS  the update is one statement
PASS  the rows written carry new numbers, not the ones read
PASS  every number written is 1 to 10000
PASS  no row the update did not answer changed
PASS  an update with no count answers 1 row
PASS  an empty update count answers 1 row
PASS  an update count of 0 answers 1 row
PASS  a negative update count answers 1 row
PASS  an update count that is not a number answers 1 row
PASS  an update count of 501 answers 500 rows
PASS  every update binds each id once, ascending
PASS  rows that share an id answer the one number written
PASS  /fortunes answers 200
PASS  /fortunes carries Server, Date and text/html; charset=utf-8
PASS  /fortunes is the expected page: the added row, sorted, escaped, the Japanese row untouched
PASS  a second /fortunes answers the same page from the reused buffer
PASS  a refused batch answers 503 with Server
PASS  the next /db is served again
PASS  no query failed but the one refused
PASS  every slot is free at the end
PASS  keys failing while the rest wait for room answer 503
PASS  its slot's next request, cached during warm-up, is answered
PASS  every slot comes back once
PASS  the entry serves on after
PASS  the full entry failed only the one request
PASS  every statement was prepared with the SQL its name stands for
